# Line endings are part of the build artifact, not a local preference.
#
# `.editorconfig` has asked for `end_of_line = lf` since the beginning, but
# nothing enforced it on checkout: `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows produced CRLF
# working trees, so the same commit built different bytes on Windows and on
# Vercel's Linux builder. That became a correctness problem on 2026-10-18, when
# the static site's CSP began allowlisting the inline theme-boot script **by
# SHA-256 hash of its exact bytes** — the CRLF build hashed differently from the
# LF build, so the hash that passed locally would have blocked the script in
# production (silently: the app still works, the theme just flashes). ADR-0008.
#
# Force LF for every text file so a Windows checkout, CI, and Vercel produce
# identical bytes. The whole index is already stored as LF, so this changes no
# committed content — it changes what a checkout writes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch their bytes.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
*.woff binary
*.ttf binary
*.apk binary
*.aab binary
*.keystore binary
*.jar binary
